          "filename": "Cutting the 375th Birthday Cake (6507420395).jpg",
          "caption": "RALEIGH, N.C. -- Governor Bev Perdue cuts a National Guard birthday cake with Pfc. Jensen Sales (left) and Airman 1st Class Phillip Mallette celebrating the founding of the guard at a ceremony at the North Carolina State Capitol, here, Dec 13.  Perdue, as governor, is the commander in chief of the North Carolina National Guard and Sales, a student and Reserve Officer Training Corps cadet at N.C. State University and Mallette, a student at University of North Carolina – Charlotte, are the most junior enlisted NCNG members.  This is the 375th anniversary of the National Guard beginning with the first muster of the militia in Massachusetts Bay Colony, Dec. 13, 1636 and serving state and nationwide today.  (U.S. Army photo by Staff Sgt. Robert Jordan, North Carolina National Guard Public Affairs)",
